{"id":"p08-l09","minutes":30,"summary":"A single wild sample (a dropped bit, an EMI spike, an encoder glitch) wrecks a linear filter’s output for N samples. Order statistics don’t care. You implement the running median and the Hampel identifier, and show both remove injected spikes while keeping steps sharp, where a moving average smears the step and only dilutes the spikes.","html":"<h2 id=\"linear-filters-spread-outliers\">Linear filters spread outliers</h2>\n<p>A moving average of length <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> turns one spike of height <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span> into a plateau of height <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> lasting <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> samples. The spike isn’t removed, only diluted. The filter also turns a clean step into a ramp <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> samples long. Linear filters can’t tell an outlier from a signal.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-running-median\">The running median</h2>\n<p>Output the <strong>median</strong> of the last <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> samples (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> odd):</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">median</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">]}</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li>An isolated spike is never the middle value, so it disappears completely, as long as fewer than half the window are outliers.</li>\n<li>A step stays a step: once more than half the window is on the new level, the output jumps. The edge is delayed by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span></span> samples (with a centred window offline, not at all) but not smeared.</li>\n<li>It’s non-linear (lesson 1), so there’s no frequency response. Its noise reduction on Gaussian noise is a little worse than a mean’s, about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.24em;vertical-align:-0.305em;\"></span><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.935em;\"><span class=\"svg-align\" style=\"top:-3.2em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.2em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"padding-left:1em;\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.895em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.2em;\"></span><span class=\"hide-tail\" style=\"min-width:1.02em;height:1.28em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"400em\" height=\"1.28em\" viewBox=\"0 0 400000 1296\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin slice\"><path d=\"M263,681c0.7,0,18,39.7,52,119\nc34,79.3,68.167,158.7,102.5,238c34.3,79.3,51.8,119.3,52.5,120\nc340,-704.7,510.7,-1060.3,512,-1067\nl0 -0\nc4.7,-7.3,11,-11,19,-11\nH40000v40H1012.3\ns-271.3,567,-271.3,567c-38.7,80.7,-84,175,-136,283c-52,108,-89.167,185.3,-111.5,232\nc-22.3,46.7,-33.8,70.3,-34.5,71c-4.7,4.7,-12.3,7,-23,7s-12,-1,-12,-1\ns-109,-253,-109,-253c-72.7,-168,-109.3,-252,-110,-252c-10.7,8,-22,16.7,-34,26\nc-22,17.3,-33.3,26,-34,26s-26,-26,-26,-26s76,-59,76,-59s76,-60,76,-60z\nM1001 80h400000v40h-400000z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.305em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> times the standard error.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-hampel-identifier\">The Hampel identifier</h2>\n<p>Sometimes you want to keep good samples untouched and replace only the bad ones. In each window, compute the median <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span></span></span></span> and the <strong>median absolute deviation</strong> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">MAD</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">median</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span></span></span></span>. For Gaussian data, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.4826</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">MAD</span></span></span></span></span> estimates σ robustly. Flag a sample as an outlier if</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6151em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.4826</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">MAD</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>typically with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6151em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span>, and replace it with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span></span></span></span>. Everything else passes through unchanged.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"median\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A step with noise and spikes: raw (blue), moving average (red) and running median (lime). Widen the window and compare the errors.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>Samples: 1.0, 1.1, 0.9, 9.0, 1.0, 1.1, 0.9 (one spike).</p>\n<ol>\n<li>A 5-point moving average around the spike gives <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0.9</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">9.0</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.0</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.9</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.58</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>The 5-point median of the same window: sorted 0.9, 0.9, 1.0, 1.1, 9.0, so the median is 1.0.</li>\n<li>Hampel with 7 points: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.0</span></span></span></span>; the deviations are 0, 0.1, 0.1, 8.0, 0, 0.1, 0.1, so MAD = 0.1 and the threshold is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.4826</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.445</span></span></span></span>. Only 9.0 is flagged; it becomes 1.0.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">median_hampel.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">running_median</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">x, k</span>):\n    h = (k - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) // <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n    xp = np.pad(x, h, mode=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;edge&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.array([np.median(xp[i:i + k]) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(x))])     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># centred window (offline)</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">hampel</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">x, k=<span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>, t=<span class=\"hljs-number\">3.0</span></span>):\n    h = (k - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) // <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n    xp = np.pad(x, h, mode=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;edge&quot;</span>)\n    y, flagged = x.copy(), np.zeros(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(x), <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">bool</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(x)):\n        w = xp[i:i + k]\n        m = np.median(w)\n        mad = np.median(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(w - m))\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(x[i] - m) &gt; t * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.4826</span> * mad:\n            y[i], flagged[i] = m, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> y, flagged\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">moving_average</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">x, k</span>):\n    h = (k - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) // <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.convolve(np.pad(x, h, mode=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;edge&quot;</span>), np.ones(k) / k, mode=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;valid&quot;</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(<span class=\"hljs-number\">9</span>)\n    n = <span class=\"hljs-number\">400</span>\n    truth = np.where(np.arange(n) &gt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>)\n    x = truth + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span> * rng.standard_normal(n)\n    spikes = rng.choice(np.r_[<span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">190</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">210</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">390</span>], <span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span>, replace=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>)\n    x[spikes] += rng.choice([-<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>], <span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span>)\n    med = running_median(x, <span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>)\n    ham, flagged = hampel(x, <span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>)\n    ma = moving_average(x, <span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>)\n    err = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> y: np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(y - truth)[np.r_[<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">195</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">205</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">395</span>]].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;worst error away from the step: moving average <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{err(ma):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span>, median <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{err(med):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span>, Hampel <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{err(ham):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span>&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> err(med) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.25</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> err(ham) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.25</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> err(ma) &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.4</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">set</span>(spikes) &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">set</span>(np.flatnonzero(flagged))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> flagged.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>() &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span>                                        <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># good samples mostly untouched</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># the step stays sharp: within one sample, the median output switches level</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> med[<span class=\"hljs-number\">198</span>] &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> med[<span class=\"hljs-number\">201</span>] &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.5</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> ma[<span class=\"hljs-number\">198</span>] &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">or</span> ma[<span class=\"hljs-number\">201</span>] &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.5</span>                            <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># the average smears it</span>\n    w = np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">9.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9</span>])\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(np.mean(w[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>]) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.58</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> np.median(w[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>]) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>\n    y, f = hampel(w, <span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> f[<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> y[<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>] == <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>                                     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># the spike is flagged and replaced by the median</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Your encoder occasionally reports bursts of three bad samples in a row. What median window do you need?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The outliers must be fewer than half the window, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8193em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">7</span></span></span></span>. Three bad samples in a window of 7 still leave four good ones, and the median is a good one.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does the Hampel filter use the MAD instead of the standard deviation?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The standard deviation is itself blown up by the outliers it should detect, so a big spike raises the threshold and hides itself. The MAD ignores up to half the samples being wild.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p08-l09\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"linear-filters-spread-outliers","title":"Linear filters spread outliers"},{"id":"the-running-median","title":"The running median"},{"id":"the-hampel-identifier","title":"The Hampel identifier"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p08-l09-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>5-point moving average of 1.1, 0.9, 9.0, 1.0, 1.1?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The spike is diluted, not removed.</p>\n","answer":2.62,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p08-l09-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Median of the same five samples?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Sorted 0.9, 1.0, 1.1, 1.1, 9.0; the spike can’t be the middle value.</p>\n","answer":1.1,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p08-l09-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Hampel threshold for MAD = 0.1 and t = 3?</p>\n","explain":"<p>t · 1.4826 · MAD.</p>\n","answer":0.44478,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p08-l09-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>A running median applied to a clean step…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Order statistics preserve edges.</p>\n","options":["adds overshoot","turns it into a ramp","removes it","keeps it sharp (possibly delayed)"],"answer":3},{"id":"p08-l09-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Minimum odd window to reject bursts of 3 consecutive outliers?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Outliers must be fewer than half.</p>\n","answer":7,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p08-l09-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The median filter is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Superposition fails.</p>\n","options":["an IIR filter","linear and time-invariant","unstable","non-linear, so it has no frequency response"],"answer":3}],"code":[{"file":"median_hampel.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\ndef running_median(x, k):\n    h = (k - 1) // 2\n    xp = np.pad(x, h, mode=\"edge\")\n    return np.array([np.median(xp[i:i + k]) for i in range(len(x))])     # centred window (offline)\n\ndef hampel(x, k=7, t=3.0):\n    h = (k - 1) // 2\n    xp = np.pad(x, h, mode=\"edge\")\n    y, flagged = x.copy(), np.zeros(len(x), bool)\n    for i in range(len(x)):\n        w = xp[i:i + k]\n        m = np.median(w)\n        mad = np.median(np.abs(w - m))\n        if np.abs(x[i] - m) > t * 1.4826 * mad:\n            y[i], flagged[i] = m, True\n    return y, flagged\n\ndef moving_average(x, k):\n    h = (k - 1) // 2\n    return np.convolve(np.pad(x, h, mode=\"edge\"), np.ones(k) / k, mode=\"valid\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(9)\n    n = 400\n    truth = np.where(np.arange(n) >= 200, 2.0, 0.0)\n    x = truth + 0.05 * rng.standard_normal(n)\n    spikes = rng.choice(np.r_[10:190, 210:390], 12, replace=False)\n    x[spikes] += rng.choice([-3, 4], 12)\n    med = running_median(x, 7)\n    ham, flagged = hampel(x, 7)\n    ma = moving_average(x, 7)\n    err = lambda y: np.abs(y - truth)[np.r_[5:195, 205:395]].max()\n    print(f\"worst error away from the step: moving average {err(ma):.2f}, median {err(med):.2f}, Hampel {err(ham):.2f}\")\n    assert err(med) < 0.25 and err(ham) < 0.25 and err(ma) > 0.4\n    assert set(spikes) <= set(np.flatnonzero(flagged))\n    assert flagged.sum() < 30                                        # good samples mostly untouched\n    # the step stays sharp: within one sample, the median output switches level\n    assert med[198] < 0.5 and med[201] > 1.5\n    assert ma[198] > 0.5 or ma[201] < 1.5                            # the average smears it\n    w = np.array([1.0, 1.1, 0.9, 9.0, 1.0, 1.1, 0.9])\n    assert abs(np.mean(w[2:7]) - 2.58) < 1e-9 and np.median(w[2:7]) == 1.0\n    y, f = hampel(w, 7)\n    assert f[3] and y[3] == 1.0                                     # the spike is flagged and replaced by the median"}]}